$ maestro-ticket job
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job: name the job: build, review, qa, live, qa-ask, plan, rule, finish, judge, design, cos
$ maestro-ticket job deploy T-1
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job: unknown job "deploy": want build, review, qa, live, qa-ask, plan, rule, finish, judge, design, cos
$ maestro-ticket job build
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job build: want one ticket id
$ maestro-ticket job build T-1 T-2
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job build: want one ticket id
$ maestro-ticket job build T-99
exit 3
stderr:
maestro-ticket: not found: ticket T-99
$ maestro-ticket job build nope
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: invalid request: bad ticket id "nope" (want T-<n>)
$ maestro-ticket job build T-1 --slots 2
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job build: --slots is for qa, live and qa-ask
$ maestro-ticket job qa T-7 --slots -1
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job: --slots must be 1 or more
$ maestro-ticket job build T-1 --approved abc1234
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job build: --approved, --drop, --drop-file and --full are for review
$ maestro-ticket job review T-1 --drop F2
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job review: --drop names the findings and --drop-file gives why: pass both
$ maestro-ticket job review T-1 --approved not-a-sha
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job review: --approved "not-a-sha": want a commit sha
$ maestro-ticket job review T-1 --drop F 2 --drop-file -
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job review: --drop "F 2": want finding ids such as F1,F3
$ maestro-ticket job plan
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job plan: send the ask on stdin, in a quoted heredoc
$ maestro-ticket job plan T-1
stdin: "x"
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job plan: takes no ticket id; give it as --ticket, and the ask on stdin
$ maestro-ticket job judge T-1 --ticket T-2
stdin: "x"
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job judge: the ids name its tickets; drop --ticket
$ maestro-ticket job judge
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job judge: want one or more ticket ids
$ maestro-ticket job live T-1
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: job live: T-1 is in_review, not todo or in_progress: nothing to do
$ maestro-ticket job build T-1
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: job build: T-1 is in_review, not todo or in_progress: nothing to do
$ maestro-ticket job review T-7
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: job review: T-7 passed review at its head: its GO stands, and QA takes it
$ maestro-ticket job build T-8
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: claimed by another holder: job build: run R-1, qa-lead's, already works on T-8
$ maestro-ticket job build T-9 --limit 25h
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job: --limit 25h0m0s: want 1s to 24h
$ maestro-ticket job build T-6
exit 0
stdout:
R-2 already going: nothing to do
$ maestro-ticket job again
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job again: want one run id, such as R-abcdefgh
$ maestro-ticket job again R-zzzzzzzz
exit 3
stderr:
maestro-ticket: not found: run R-zzzzzzzz
$ maestro-ticket job again R-3
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: not allowed for this actor: job again: run R-3 is reviewer's
$ maestro-ticket job again R-4
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job again: run R-4 isn't a job's
$ maestro-ticket job again R-2
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: job again: run R-2 is running, D into its 2h limit: wait for its end, or end it with maestro-ticket stop R-2
$ maestro-ticket resume
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: resume: want one run id, such as R-abcdefgh
$ maestro-ticket resume nope
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: resume: want one run id, such as R-abcdefgh
$ maestro-ticket resume R-zzzzzzzz
exit 3
stderr:
maestro-ticket: not found: run R-zzzzzzzz
$ maestro-ticket resume R-3
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: not allowed for this actor: resume: run R-3 is reviewer's: only the bot that launched it resumes it
$ maestro-ticket resume R-2
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: resume: run R-2 is running, D into its 2h limit: wait for its end, or end it with maestro-ticket stop R-2
$ maestro-ticket resume R-5 --died
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: status conflict: resume --died: run R-5 done, it didn't die: a hung or failed run goes to whoever handed you the job
$ maestro-ticket resume R-6
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: resume: send the answer on stdin, in a quoted heredoc
$ maestro-ticket resume R-5
stdin: "go on"
exit 0
stdout:
resume: T-1 is in_review now: run R-5's session has nothing left to do there: acked R-5
$ maestro-ticket job build T-9
exit 2
stderr:
maestro-ticket: job: set MAESTRO_TICKET_ACTOR (or --actor) to your bot id: a run's result goes back to whoever launched it
$ maestro-ticket job build T-9
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: refused: the kill switch is on: stopped: maestro/STOP is set: start no run
$ maestro-ticket job build T-9
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: refused: a usage limit holds: paused: usage limit, until T: start no run until then
$ maestro-ticket resume R-6
stdin: "x"
exit 4
stderr:
maestro-ticket: refused: a usage limit holds: paused: usage limit, until T: start no run until then
